    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Let \\( X \\) be the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan.\n\nFirst, we need to convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to US dollars. We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars, so:\n\\[\n\\text{Cost of the painting in US dollars} = \\frac{\\text{Cost in Namibian dollars}}{7} = \\frac{105}{7} = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n\\]\n\nNext, we convert US dollars to Chinese yuan. We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan, so:\n\\[\n\\text{Cost of the painting in Chinese yuan} = 15 \\text{ US dollars} \\times 6 \\text{ Chinese yuan per US dollar} = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n\\]\n\nThus, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
