    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to US dollars:**\n   We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars. Therefore, the cost of the painting in US dollars is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{\\text{Cost in Namibian dollars}}{7} = \\frac{105}{7} = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert the cost of the painting from US dollars to Chinese yuan:**\n   We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan. Therefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = \\text{Cost in US dollars} \\times 6 = 15 \\times 6 = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\boxed{90}.",
