    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to US dollars and then from US dollars to Chinese yuan.\n\n1. **Convert Namibian dollars to US dollars:**\n   We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars. Therefore, the cost of the painting in US dollars can be calculated as follows:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{\\text{Cost in Namibian dollars}}{7} = \\frac{105}{7} = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert US dollars to Chinese yuan:**\n   We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan. Therefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan can be calculated as follows:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = \\text{Cost in US dollars} \\times 6 = 15 \\times 6 = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
